<title>SWEDEN: Skanska 1996 profit soars to 5.17 bln skr.</title>
<headline>Skanska 1996 profit soars to 5.17 bln skr.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish construction company Skanska AB posted 1996 earnings on Tuesday.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		5,172    vs  2,573</p>
<p> Sales				    47,872    vs 38,608</p>
<p> New orders			     52,500    vs 44,029</p>
<p> Proposed Dividend (crowns)	     10    vs	5</p>
<p> Earnings per share(crowns)	     32.35 vs     12.80</p>
<p> Operating costs			44,168    vs 35,400</p>
<p> New appraisals		    CREDIT 49    vs	2 CHARGE</p>
<p> Investment, development properties  790    vs    532</p>
<p> Interests in associate companies    773    vs    477</p>
<p> Operating income before deprec.   5,316    vs  4,215</p>
<p> Depreciation			    1,198    vs    983</p>
<p> Operating profit			4,118    vs  3,232</p>
<p> Dividends				   461    vs    350</p>
<p> Interest revenues			 486    vs    627</p>
<p> Interest expenses		     1,384    vs  1,519</p>
<p> Exchange differences on loans	  12    vs	7</p>
<p> Sale of shares/participations     1,760    vs     25</p>
<p> Other financial items	    CHARGE 8    vs     14 CHARGE</p>
<p> Shr of associate fin items   CHARGE 273    vs    135 CHARGE</p>
<p> Taxes					 813    vs    692</p>
<p> Minorities				  179    vs    271</p>
<p> Net profit				4,074    vs  1,610</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuter poll of 12 analysts showed expectations of a profit after financial items, including capital gains, of 4.93 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
